       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is double the maximum daily dose. It carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. Entering it as written could put the patient at real risk.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If the dose was a typo or a mix-up between total daily and per-dose amounts**, give me the intended dose and I'll enter it right away. For example, 800 mg four times daily is 3,200 mg/day, the upper limit.\n- **If you think there's a special reason for this dose**, please discuss it with a clinical pharmacist or the attending. They can verify it and enter it through the appropriate override process.\n- **If the goal is stronger pain or anti-inflammatory control**, I can enter a different or additional agent, such as scheduled acetaminophen. Choosing it is your call."
